{title: For a Thousand Tongues}
{artist: C. Michael Pilato, Charles Wesley}
{key: Bb}
{time: 6/8}
{tempo: 74}

Verse 1
All-gracious Master, [Cm]glorious God,
[Gm]Give me the words to proclaim.
[Bm]Spread through the whole earth &mdash; [Cm]here and abroad &mdash;
The [Gm]honor of Your holy [F]name.
[Em]Father, You give me the [Bm]choice,
But [Em]Your grace compels me to [Bm]lift up my [F/A]voice.
[Gm7]If I was mute, [Em]I'd still make [Bm]joyful noise [F]to the King.
[Em]Oh, [Cm7]for a thousand [F]tongues to sing!

Verse 2
Jesus, your name calms the deepest of fears.
You bid every sorrow to cease.
Your mercy is music in this sinner's ears&mdash;
Your love is the source of my peace.
Savior, You knew all along
That you'd trade perfection for all I'd do wrong.
Lord, may my life make a beautiful song [Em]to the King.
Oh, for a thousand tongues to sing!

Verse 3
Oh, for a thousand tongues to [F]sing [Em]my great Redeemer's praise!
Sing [Bm]of the glories of my King; the triumph of His [F]grace!

Verse 4
[Bm]Jesus you've broken the [Cm]power of sin.
Your [Gm]blood sets the prisoners [Em]free.
[Bm]Dying you saved us, then [Cm]rising again
Accomplished [Gm]supreme victory!

Verse 5
[F]Oh, for a thousand [Em]tongues to sing our [Bm]great Redeemer's [F]praise!
Sing of the glories [Em]of our King; the [Bm]triumph of His [F]grace!
Your church in heaven and [Em]earth below, this [Bm]sacrifice we [F]bring!

Verse 6
Oh, for a thousand tongues to [Emmaj7]sing.
Oh, for a thousand [F]tongues to [Emmaj7]sing.
Oh, for a thousand [F]tongues to [Em]sing.

Verse 7
Spirit of God, fill this [Bm]place.
[Em]Write on our hearts songs of [Bm]mercy and [F/A]grace.
[Gm7]Oh, God, we're desperate [Em]to give every [Bm]praise [F]to the King.
[Em]Oh, [Gm]for a thousand [F]tongues to sing!
[Em]Oh, [Gm]for a thousand [F]tongues to sing!
[Cm7]Oh, [Gm]for a thousand [F]tongues to sing!
